From 98f96ccf207147757db6278fd8ca965f758e525b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:50:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(adaptive): a 2D Adaptive takes a start point and an exit
 point

The start point is the seed of the HSM plan. The helix or the plunge
goes down there on each level, through the same entry law, and the plan
grows the cleared area from that bore under its engagement law. The exit
point ends the last pass of each level: the tool runs back along the
same posted moves in reverse, over one round of the outer wall at most,
to the point nearest the pick, and climbs out there. Reversed moves cut
no new material and cross no feed.

A point that the plan cannot hold is refused by name and nothing is cut:
a start outside the area the tool centre reaches, a helix without room,
a point in a "Do not touch" keep-out, an exit too far from the closing
ride, a plan from the start that keeps an overload or falls back to the
Offset rings, and (at the door) a tilted op, the Trochoidal method, Pass
starts at Inside or Outside, a rest pass, or a start with a Ramp or Arc
entry.

Without a pick no new code runs, so every earlier path is the same to
the byte. The picks ride the shared picks field (#3339): the undoable
EditOperationParams, the file, the stamp and MCP edit_operation. The
Lead in / Lead out tab draws the Start point and Exit point groups, and
the viewport pick takes the 2D Adaptive.

Fixes #3327

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
